    "definition": "Improvement in the follower's mean lap time after the car DIRECTLY ahead pits, measured over W raced laps either side of the stop, for followers within PROXIMITY seconds. Positive means the follower got faster once the air cleared. Raw values also contain whatever the follower's own lap times were doing anyway across the comparison, so corrected values subtract the measured lap-to-lap trend over the span between window centres. Over these three seasons that trend is NEGATIVE (p50 -0.02 s/lap): burning fuel outweighs ageing the tyre, so the correction lowers the estimate and the raw figure is an upper bound, not a lower one.",
